# gnome-settings-daemon -- the seventeen small daemons that make a GNOME session
# behave: colour, power, keyboard, media keys, sound, printing, rfkill and the
# rest. gnome-session starts them; without them the shell runs and nothing
# responds.
#
# GNOME 48 series, BLFS 12.4, which pins 48.1.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/gnome-settings-daemon/48/gnome-settings-daemon-48.1.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=3860a2ea214dcbcb6600ae7a1e3358a5389215087bc3e4a47cee3f87baee062e
SRC_DIR=gnome-settings-daemon-48.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -Dsystemd=false -Delogind=true IS A MANDATORY PAIR, AND THIS PACKAGE IS THE
# ONE THAT GETS ELOGIND RIGHT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# meson.build:119-131:
#
#     enable_systemd = get_option('systemd')     # defaults TRUE
#     enable_elogind = get_option('elogind')     # defaults FALSE
#
#     if enable_systemd and enable_elogind
#       error('Only systemd or elogind support should be activated')
#     elif enable_systemd
#       systemd_dep = dependency('systemd', ...)         # no systemd.pc here
#       libsystemd_dep = dependency('libsystemd', ...)
#     elif enable_elogind
#       elogind_dep = dependency('libelogind', version: '>= 209', required: true)
#
# BOTH must be set, and in opposite directions: leaving systemd at its default
# while enabling elogind is an explicit error(), and leaving both alone asks
# pkg-config for a systemd.pc that elogind does not ship.
#
# This is the FIRST package in this chain where elogind is a first-class named
# choice rather than something arrived at through elogind's libsystemd.pc
# compatibility symlink. gnome-session takes dependency('libsystemd') with no
# option and no guard and gets elogind by accident; this one asks for
# libelogind by its own name. The difference is entirely in whether upstream
# thought about it, and it is worth seeing the two side by side.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WACOM IS NOT AN OPTION. IT IS DECIDED BY THE ARCHITECTURE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# meson.build:173 is
#
#     enable_wacom = host_is_linux_not_s390
#
# There is no -Dwacom. On x86_64 and aarch64 this is unconditionally TRUE, so
# libwacom is a HARD dependency with no flag to decline it -- stronger than a
# defaulted exclusion, which at least has a switch. It is declared as a plain
# runtime dependency for that reason.
#
# It is also an upstream arch conditional, which means this recipe would behave
# differently on s390 -- irrelevant here, since this tree builds two
# architectures and both satisfy it, but recorded so that "verified" is not
# quietly standing in for "verified on the arches we build".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERY OTHER OPTION IS LEFT AT ITS DEFAULT, AND EVERY ONE WAS CHECKED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# All of these default TRUE and each removes a plugin from the build when off
# (plugins/meson.build:21-52), so a missing dependency would cost a feature
# rather than fail the build. Each was confirmed present in this tree before
# being left alone -- a defaulted requirement is a silent one:
#
#   alsa               alsa-lib          (:139 asserts it on Linux anyway)
#   gudev              libgudev          (:157 asserts it on Linux anyway, and
#                                        wayland and wacom both assert it too)
#   cups               cups 2.4.12       gates BOTH the cups plugin and
#                                        print-notifications
#   colord             colord 1.4.8      gates the color plugin
#   smartcard          gcr 4.4.0         via gck-2, since -Dgcr3 is false
#   wwan               gcr + ModemManager 1.24.2 (mm-glib)
#   network_manager    NetworkManager 1.54.0
#   rfkill, usb-protection, wayland      no new packages
#
# -Dgcr3 is left FALSE, its default, which selects gck-2/gcr-4 (meson.build
# :228-233). This tree has gcr 4.4.0 and no gcr3 in the desktop path, so the
# default is also the correct choice rather than merely the quiet one.
#
# The unconditional set is large and every member of it is already here:
# gnome-desktop-3.0 (:104 -- the THIRD consumer of the legacy library, after
# gnome-session and the two counted in the gnome-desktop reversal),
# gtk+-x11-3.0 (:107 -- resolves only because gtk3 was built with its X11
# backend in another chain's recipe), gweather4, libcanberra-gtk3,
# libgeoclue-2.0, libnotify, libpulse-mainloop-glib, polkit-gobject-1,
# upower-glib, x11 and xfixes.
MESON_ARGS="-Dsystemd=false -Delogind=true"
